and one local father has made it his  life's mission to help cut down on the  number of people taking their own lives  reggie burton knows the issue all too  well his son avery died by suicide  victoria saha joining us now with more  on the story and also advice that burton  has for other parents yesterday's burton  is a parent who knows too well the  heartache he says this is such a  sensitive topic but an important one  that needs to be discussed so families  can recognize the silent cries for help  graduation a momentous time for students  and everyone around them sometimes that  celebration is just a precursor to a  stressful event burton's son avery had  the world ahead of him in may of 2017 he  graduated from unlv with the hopes of  becoming a doctor and then he realized  it wasn't what he actually wanted or at  least he didn't think he wants it and  that's what spurred the major depressive  episode just two months later that  depressive state led avery to take his  own life so this is a kid that was used  to fixing  problems but this was just one problem  that he couldn't solve burton says  although his family was aware that avery  was going through a tough time he says  avery was very good at hiding the extent  of it which he says is a common thing  among those struggling with mental  illness families default to  love they want to try to love the  problem away and what we need to try to  understand and the lesson we learned is  that love's not enough and experts say  it's okay for family and friends to take  that first step to start the  conversation having a really hard  conversation and if there's any notice  any change that the parents notice that  is different from their norm  then you know that's that's an area of  concern and certainly needs to be  addressed a conversation that can  hopefully turn the outcome around the  surviving family members my heart goes  out to them because they have a lot of  questions and not a lot of answers  since avery's death burton says he  started a foundation in his son's name  aimed at helping those struggling you  can find more about the avery burton  foundation on our website at  8newsnow.com ryan
 

